=== task: mcq medium
title: A huge, sparse graph
prompt: A road network has 1,000,000 junctions, and each junction has about 4 roads. Which way of storing it fits best?
* An adjacency list :: Right. It needs space for about 1,000,000 vertices plus 4,000,000 neighbour entries, O(V + E).
- An adjacency matrix :: That would need 1,000,000 × 1,000,000 boxes, a million million, almost all 0.
